  "name": "Jehoiada (The Priest Who Guided King Joash of Judah)",
  "title": "The High Priest Who Preserved David's Royal Line",
  "era": "divided-kingdom",
  "lifespan": "c. 880–800 BC",
  "summary": "Jehoiada was the high priest in Jerusalem during Queen Athaliah's tyrannical rule. He hid the young Joash in the temple for six years and led a successful coup against Athaliah to restore the Davidic royal line. Throughout his life, he guided King Joash and led the people back to worshiping the Lord, and he was honored with a burial among the kings when he died at the age of 130.",
